Metrics List:
- {"name": "container_ulimits_soft", "type": "gauge", "description": "Soft ulimit values for the container root process."}
- {"name": "container_fs_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of bytes that are consumed by the container on this filesystem."}
- {"name": "container_spec_memory_limit_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Memory limit for the container."}
- {"name": "container_fs_limit_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of bytes that can be consumed by the container on this filesystem."}
- {"name": "container_memory_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Current memory usage in bytes, including all memory regardless of when it was accessed"}
Question: Show the filesystem usage and limit bytes for all containers of the auth service.

Metrics List:
- {"name": "node_sockstat_UDP_mem", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of UDP sockets in state mem."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_TCP_mem", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of TCP sockets in state mem."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_UDP_mem_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of UDP sockets in state mem_bytes."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_UDP_inuse", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of UDP sockets in state inuse."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_TCP_mem_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of TCP sockets in state mem_bytes."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_TCP_inuse", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of TCP sockets in state inuse."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_TCP_alloc", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of TCP sockets in state alloc."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_RAW_inuse", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of RAW sockets in state inuse."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_FRAG_memory", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of FRAG sockets in state memory."}
- {"name": "node_sockstat_FRAG_inuse", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of FRAG sockets in state inuse."}
- {"name": "kube_replicaset_spec_replicas", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Number of desired pods for a ReplicaSet."}
- {"name": "kube_deployment_spec_replicas", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Number of desired pods for a deployment."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_status_ready_time", "type": "gauge", "description": "Readiness achieved time in unix timestamp for a pod."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_status_ready", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Describes whether the pod is ready to serve requests."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_status_container_ready_time", "type": "gauge", "description": "Readiness achieved time in unix timestamp for a pod containers."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_container_status_terminated", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Describes whether the container is currently in terminated state."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_container_status_running", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Describes whether the container is currently in running state."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_container_status_ready", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Describes whether the containers readiness check succeeded."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_container_resource_requests", "type": "gauge", "description": "The number of requested request resource by a container. It is recommended to use the kube_pod_resource_requests metric exposed by kube-scheduler instead, as it is more precise."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_container_resource_limits", "type": "gauge", "description": "The number of requested limit resource by a container. It is recommended to use the kube_pod_resource_limits metric exposed by kube-scheduler instead, as it is more precise."}
Question: Use data from the past hour to perform a linear prediction of the number of UDP sockets in the mem state on nodes hosting RabbitMQ pods for the next 5 minutes.
